    "chapterId": 54,
    "fileId": 50733,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Goblet cell adenocarcinoma of appendix",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Low-grade (G1) goblet cell adenocarcinoma shows cohesive and smooth-contoured clusters of tumour cells with goblet-like intracellular mucin resembling intestinal crypts (upper panel). High-grade (G3) goblet cell adenocarcinoma shows loss of most cohesive clusters with aggregates of tumour cells having irregular contours, single-cell infiltration, stromal desmoplasia, with marked nuclear atypia, and pleomorphism (lower panel).",
    "source": "Laura H. Tang",
